# 34. Private Data / Untrusted Data / Outbound Action Separation

## 34.1 The Profile Trust Rule

No single profile may combine all three of:

1. access to private data or credentials
2. exposure to untrusted content
3. ability to communicate outward

Two of three is acceptable. Three is not. This combination creates a direct data-exfiltration path.

## 34.2 Profile trust table

| Profile | Private data | Untrusted content | Outbound | Egress policy |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| personal | yes | no | limited | strict allowlist |
| research | no | yes | web read only | open web, no credentials, no send tools |
| automation | scoped | limited | specific APIs | strict allowlist |
| high-risk | temporary | no | via broker only | broker only |

