# 71. MCP / Skill Vetting Checklist

No unreviewed MCP. No unreviewed skill. Before adding any MCP server or skill:

```text
[ ] What code runs? Where does it come from? (repo, publisher, commit pinned?)
[ ] What credentials can it see? (env, files, Hermes secret scope)
[ ] What network access does it need? (domains, direction, justify each)
[ ] What filesystem access does it need? (paths, justify each)
[ ] What tools does it expose? Any that send data outward?
[ ] Does it survive the profile trust rule? (§34 — no private data + untrusted content + outbound in one profile)
[ ] Which threat(s) from §4.2 does this help with — or worsen?
[ ] What is the blast radius if it is malicious or compromised?
[ ] How do we remove/rotate if we revoke it?
[ ] Re-review after every version bump.
```

A skill/MCP that fails the trust rule must run in the high-risk profile or not at all.

