## 73.1 One-Person Review Checklist (v0.3)

The fifteen-expert review is overkill for one person. Use this one-page checklist instead — it gives most of the value:

```text
SECURITY REVIEW (one page, run before any significant change)

1. BOUNDARY: Which security boundary does this sit behind? Can the agent bypass it?
2. THREAT: Which threat(s) from §4.2 does this reduce? (If none — why add it?)
3. TRUST RULE: Does it create a profile with private data + untrusted content + outbound? (§34)
4. CREDENTIALS: What new credentials exist? Where do they live? Who/what can read them?
5. WORST CASE: If this component is compromised, what is the blast radius?
6. RECOVERY: If this fails or vanishes, can we still recover? (escrow covers it?)
7. EGRESS: What network access does it need? Is it allowlisted and logged?
8. COST: What does it cost money-wise, and does it have a cap?
9. MONITORING: How do we know when it misbehaves? (heartbeat, canary, alert?)
10. ROLLBACK: How do we undo this change safely?
11. TESTING: What proves it works? (rebuild test, break-glass test, egress test)
12. DOCS: Are the data map, decisions log, and threat model updated?
```

For genuinely major changes, the full fifteen-expert list (§74) remains available.

