# 75. Golden Security Rules

### v0.1 rules (1–20)

1. No public VNC.
2. No unnecessary public SSH.
3. No Hermes as root.
4. No secrets in Git.
5. No unrestricted sudo.
6. No unrestricted agent egress.
7. No profile combining unrestricted private data + untrusted content + outbound communication.
8. No privileged credentials in Hermes.
9. No agent-controlled final approval.
10. No single recovery dependency.
11. No backup without restore testing.
12. No single backup credential with destructive privileges.
13. No unreviewed MCP.
14. No unreviewed skill.
15. No unrestricted browser session to sensitive personal accounts.
16. No open messaging gateway.
17. No unaudited privileged action.
18. No assumption that Cloudflare alone establishes application identity.
19. No dependence on the VPS for all monitoring.
20. No dependence on the VPS for recovery.

### v0.2 additions (21–28)

21. No profile combines private data, untrusted content, and outbound communication.
22. Outbound traffic is default-deny.
23. Level 3 and 4 credentials never enter an agent context. Only the broker holds them.
24. Approvals are enforced outside the agent, on an out-of-band channel.
25. Recovery secrets are escrowed offline.
26. Monitoring has an external heartbeat.
27. Every API key and profile has a spend cap.
28. Break-glass access exists and is tested.
29. Every new component names the threat it reduces.

### v0.3 additions (30–31)

30. Level 4 credentials never live on the VPS — not even in the broker.
31. Browser profiles and cookies are never included in backups.

